  "story-1": {
    "src": "/lesson-1/audio/narration/story-1.mp3",
    "text": "Tokugawa Ieyasu made Edo Castle his home in 1590. In 1603, he established his government as shogun—Japan’s military ruler.\n\nThe emperor remained in Kyoto. Around Edo’s government, a growing city needed homes, shops, streets, and aqueducts to carry water.",
